+
+// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the park (no reachable target / no contact mark)
+//
+// The gentle settle needs the blow's time AND a target frame within ±35 % of the loop's own pace. Two cases fall
+// outside it (contact-probe, lane D 2026-11-06: kill contacts of most cards struck mid-idle):
+//   - the attacker's attack has no 'contact' mark (a thrown / fired / dashing strike: its flight is its own), so
+//     only an estimate is known — the attack's 'impact' / 'release' mark (the blow leaves), strikeLeadIn;
+//   - a contact time is known but no target frame is in reach of the stretch.
+// Then the loop is steered onto the nearest target frame it can reach by the lead (holds × PARK_FAST … × 1), and
+// PARKED there: the body holds that frame — a held breath before the blow — until the struck pose starts (the
+// settle's usual ends), at most PARK_MAX_MS past the lead (then the loop simply plays on). A target frame reached
+// as late as possible keeps the hold short; the frame is one the struck poses continue (KK-4), so the contact
+// reads local instead of snapping from mid-idle.
+
+/** Holds may shrink to this share while the loop hurries onto a target frame before a blow (park): ≥ 40 ms per
+ * frame for the usual 100–130 ms idle holds (HA-2), every frame still shown in order. */
+export const PARK_FAST = 0.4;
+/** Longest show time (ms) a parked body waits past the lead for the blow before its loop plays on. */
+export const PARK_MAX_MS = 1000;
